(1, '27', 27, 'class="av-devanagari">तान्समीक्ष्य स कौन्तेयः सर्वान्बन्धूनवस्थितान्  ।
कृपया परयाविष्टो विषीदन्निदमब्रवीत् ॥ २७ ॥

<div', 'class="av-verse_text">tān samīkṣya sa kaunteyaḥ
sarvān bandhūn avasthitān
kṛpayā parayāviṣṭo
viṣīdann idam abravīt

<div', 'class="av-synonyms">tān — all of them; samīkṣya — after seeing; saḥ — he; kaunteyaḥ — the son of Kuntī; sarvān — all kinds of; bandhūn — relatives; avasthitān — situated; kṛpayā — by compassion; parayā — of a high grade; āviṣṭaḥ — overwhelmed; viṣīdan — while lamenting; idam — thus; abravīt — spoke.

<div', 'class="av-translation">When the son of Kuntī, Arjuna, saw all these different grades of friends and relatives, he became overwhelmed with compassion and spoke thus.

TEXT 26TEXT 28

